1
00:00:02,360 --> 00:00:04,737
Now besides the Single Responsibility

2
00:00:04,769 --> 00:00:07,885
Principle, there is one other core principle

3
00:00:08,447 --> 00:00:10,246
you should be aware of when working with

4
00:00:10,310 --> 00:00:13,008
classes, especially in the context of clean

5
00:00:13,041 --> 00:00:13,330
code.

6
00:00:14,245 --> 00:00:16,237
And that's the Open-Closed Principle.

7
00:00:16,815 --> 00:00:20,027
The Open-Closed Principle says that a class

8
00:00:20,027 --> 00:00:23,833
should be open for extension but closed for

9
00:00:23,865 --> 00:00:24,652
modification.

10
00:00:25,391 --> 00:00:26,387
Now what does this mean?

11
00:00:27,254 --> 00:00:30,130
Here is an example. Now again, it's just a

12
00:00:30,130 --> 00:00:32,604
dummy class without actual code because

13
00:00:32,636 --> 00:00:34,355
again, it is more about the general

14
00:00:34,548 --> 00:00:37,439
architecture of your classes, the API of

15
00:00:37,439 --> 00:00:38,066
your classes.

16
00:00:38,740 --> 00:00:40,106
And what we can see is that we have a

17
00:00:40,106 --> 00:00:41,182
Printer class

18
00:00:41,793 --> 00:00:43,801
which actually has different methods for

19
00:00:43,801 --> 00:00:47,560
printing PDF documents, web documents, so

20
00:00:47,736 --> 00:00:50,917
probably HTML pages, and also printPage

21
00:00:51,094 --> 00:00:53,488
which maybe prints real pages in the real

22
00:00:53,664 --> 00:00:53,809
world.

23
00:00:54,730 --> 00:00:57,692
We also have a verifyData method which

24
00:00:57,951 --> 00:01:01,270
probably is called internally to verify the

25
00:01:01,270 --> 00:01:03,831
data from any of these print methods here.

26
00:01:04,919 --> 00:01:07,014
Now what's the problem with this class?

27
00:01:08,586 --> 00:01:11,713
It basically needs to grow whenever we add

28
00:01:11,761 --> 00:01:12,922
new functionality.

29
00:01:13,824 --> 00:01:17,339
If we also want to print Word documents or

30
00:01:17,453 --> 00:01:20,509
Microsoft Excel spreadsheets, we need to add

31
00:01:20,606 --> 00:01:21,205
a new method.

32
00:01:21,862 --> 00:01:24,074
Whenever we need to call a new method

33
00:01:24,266 --> 00:01:27,407
besides verifyData from our print methods,

34
00:01:27,712 --> 00:01:30,613
we have to add that logic to all the print

35
00:01:30,613 --> 00:01:31,013
methods.

36
00:01:31,718 --> 00:01:34,170
So this Printer class might have one

37
00:01:34,267 --> 00:01:37,648
responsibility. It's about printing data and

38
00:01:37,648 --> 00:01:39,091
about generating output,

39
00:01:39,972 --> 00:01:42,681
but it actually is not closed for

40
00:01:42,713 --> 00:01:43,610
modification.

41
00:01:44,524 --> 00:01:47,008
We need to go back to it all the time

42
00:01:47,328 --> 00:01:50,550
whenever we add new functionality. It's not

43
00:01:50,550 --> 00:01:51,575
very extensible.

44
00:01:52,137 --> 00:01:54,450
And therefore it violates the Open-Closed

45
00:01:54,546 --> 00:01:56,778
Principle because it should be closed for

46
00:01:56,795 --> 00:01:59,027
modification, which this one isn't.

47
00:01:59,766 --> 00:02:01,837
Now this might remind you of this

48
00:02:02,030 --> 00:02:03,990
polymorphism example from before

49
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:07,378
where we had these different delivery

50
00:02:07,410 --> 00:02:10,189
classes for delivering goods

51
00:02:11,168 --> 00:02:13,899
and where we had duplicate code before we

52
00:02:13,899 --> 00:02:15,264
utilized polymorphism.

53
00:02:16,725 --> 00:02:19,745
Indeed, the Open-Closed Principle is kind of

54
00:02:19,761 --> 00:02:20,789
related to that.

55
00:02:21,531 --> 00:02:24,053
Instead of having this Printer class here,

56
00:02:25,653 --> 00:02:28,014
it would be preferable to have code like

57
00:02:28,094 --> 00:02:28,304
this,

58
00:02:29,550 --> 00:02:32,203
to have, for example, a Printer interface

59
00:02:32,737 --> 00:02:34,290
and then a base class

60
00:02:34,824 --> 00:02:37,397
which just has this verifyData method which

61
00:02:37,510 --> 00:02:39,662
probably is shared amongst all classes.

62
00:02:40,731 --> 00:02:43,029
But then all these specific subclasses

63
00:02:43,239 --> 00:02:45,975
implement this Printer interface which

64
00:02:46,234 --> 00:02:47,855
forces them to have a print method

65
00:02:48,424 --> 00:02:50,099
and they extend the base class to then all

66
00:02:50,115 --> 00:02:51,026
have a print method

67
00:02:52,896 --> 00:02:55,449
which then just does different things

68
00:02:55,722 --> 00:02:57,376
depending on which class it is.

69
00:02:58,773 --> 00:03:01,101
The advantage is that the base class, the

70
00:03:01,101 --> 00:03:04,312
printer implementation, can be closed for

71
00:03:04,376 --> 00:03:06,014
modification at some point.

72
00:03:06,865 --> 00:03:09,434
Once the API is finished, we close it.

73
00:03:10,173 --> 00:03:12,148
Of course, we can still edit it if we need

74
00:03:12,180 --> 00:03:15,166
to fix bugs, but we don't need to edit it

75
00:03:15,375 --> 00:03:17,928
all the time just to add new features.

76
00:03:18,442 --> 00:03:21,716
Instead, to add new features, we extend it.

77
00:03:22,695 --> 00:03:24,492
And that of course is what the Open-Closed

78
00:03:24,540 --> 00:03:27,076
Principle says. A class should be open for

79
00:03:27,108 --> 00:03:27,879
extension.

80
00:03:28,617 --> 00:03:30,671
And we can build brand new Printer

81
00:03:30,735 --> 00:03:34,379
subclasses like for example a Word or an

82
00:03:34,475 --> 00:03:37,219
ExcelPrinter which just extends the

83
00:03:37,219 --> 00:03:40,204
PrinterImplementation class and implements

84
00:03:40,269 --> 00:03:43,157
the Printer class which then just forces us

85
00:03:43,157 --> 00:03:45,451
to add a specific print method again.

86
00:03:46,269 --> 00:03:48,337
This is how we can follow the Open-Closed

87
00:03:48,369 --> 00:03:48,818
Principle.

88
00:03:49,651 --> 00:03:52,440
Now, why does the Open-Closed Principle help

89
00:03:52,440 --> 00:03:53,466
us with clean code?

90
00:03:54,124 --> 00:03:56,336
Or why does it help us with clean code more

91
00:03:56,544 --> 00:03:58,035
than maybe some other principles?

92
00:03:59,414 --> 00:04:02,507
Because this extensibility ensures small

93
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:03,165
classes

94
00:04:03,742 --> 00:04:07,012
automatically because otherwise, if we don't

95
00:04:07,044 --> 00:04:07,573
extend,

96
00:04:08,711 --> 00:04:11,885
if we stick to the big do-it-all class

97
00:04:12,013 --> 00:04:15,043
instead, then this class, this Printer class

98
00:04:15,299 --> 00:04:18,407
keeps on growing and growing the more ways

99
00:04:18,439 --> 00:04:19,456
of printing we add.

100
00:04:20,844 --> 00:04:22,538
On the other hand, if we have multiple

101
00:04:22,554 --> 00:04:25,249
smaller classes, we can add more and more

102
00:04:25,298 --> 00:04:27,533
features without getting growing and growing

103
00:04:27,631 --> 00:04:28,182
classes.

104
00:04:29,910 --> 00:04:32,622
So it helps us with smaller focused classes

105
00:04:32,912 --> 00:04:35,915
and it can help prevent code duplication. It

106
00:04:35,915 --> 00:04:37,464
can help us stay DRY,

107
00:04:38,659 --> 00:04:40,890
don't repeat yourself. The Open-Closed

108
00:04:40,922 --> 00:04:42,636
Principle helps us with that as well.

109
00:04:43,402 --> 00:04:46,046
Because just as shown in the polymorphism

110
00:04:46,046 --> 00:04:49,267
example, we have all these classes and we

111
00:04:49,316 --> 00:04:51,623
avoid extra code duplication.

112
00:04:53,081 --> 00:04:56,271
And of course, both aspects, small classes

113
00:04:56,447 --> 00:04:59,908
and DRY code, are what clean code also is

114
00:04:59,924 --> 00:05:00,405
about

115
00:05:00,966 --> 00:05:02,264
because that helps us with

116
00:05:02,793 --> 00:05:04,492
readability and of course also

117
00:05:04,492 --> 00:05:05,565
maintainability.

118
00:05:06,382 --> 00:05:08,914
But especially the readability and the

119
00:05:09,027 --> 00:05:11,895
understandability of the code is what helps

120
00:05:12,152 --> 00:05:14,459
us as humans if we analyze code.

121
00:05:15,213 --> 00:05:17,923
Instead of diving into this large class and

122
00:05:18,084 --> 00:05:20,938
looking for the right method we need, we can

123
00:05:21,050 --> 00:05:24,017
just jump to the specific Printer class we

124
00:05:24,017 --> 00:05:27,048
need and it's crystal clear what it does and

125
00:05:27,145 --> 00:05:29,358
all the code in there is crystal clear.

126
00:05:29,967 --> 00:05:31,876
Of course, if we then also follow all the

127
00:05:31,956 --> 00:05:34,217
other rules for the actual code which is

128
00:05:34,217 --> 00:05:36,767
written in there, like for naming and for

129
00:05:36,767 --> 00:05:37,473
our methods.

130
00:05:38,467 --> 00:05:40,760
But that is why the Open-Closed Principle

131
00:05:40,809 --> 00:05:41,466
matters here.
